<figure class="fulfillment-example" aria-label="Illustrative fulfillment data: five of six delivered shipments are on time, but only two of four orders are complete by January 31">
  <div class="example-head">
    <span class="example-label">Illustrative fulfillment data</span>
    <strong class="example-title">Four orders. Two fulfilled on time.</strong>
    <p>All <span class="qf-figure">4</span> orders were due Jan <span class="qf-figure">31</span>. Snapshot: end of Feb <span class="qf-figure">3</span>. Each shipment carries one item.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ledger-head" aria-hidden="true">
    <span>Order</span>
    <span>Item shipments</span>
    <span>Order result</span>
  </div>
  <ol class="order-ledger" aria-label="Four eligible orders, evaluated against the original January 31 promise">
    <li class="order-row">
      <strong class="order-id">A100</strong>
      <div class="shipments" role="group" aria-label="Two item shipments">
        <span class="shipment on-time"><span class="shipment-date">Jan 30</span><span class="shipment-state">On time</span></span>
        <span class="shipment on-time"><span class="shipment-date">Jan 31</span><span class="shipment-state">On time</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="order-result">
        <strong class="result-on-time">Complete on time</strong>
        <span><span class="qf-figure">2 / 2</span> items delivered</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="order-row">
      <strong class="order-id">A101</strong>
      <div class="shipments" role="group" aria-label="Two item shipments">
        <span class="shipment on-time"><span class="shipment-date">Jan 31</span><span class="shipment-state">On time</span></span>
        <span class="shipment late"><span class="shipment-date">Feb 2</span><span class="shipment-state">Late</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="order-result">
        <strong class="result-late">Complete late</strong>
        <span><span class="qf-figure">2 / 2</span> items delivered</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="order-row">
      <strong class="order-id">A102</strong>
      <div class="shipments" role="group" aria-label="One item delivered; one item still undelivered">
        <span class="shipment on-time"><span class="shipment-date">Jan 31</span><span class="shipment-state">On time</span></span>
        <span class="shipment pending"><span class="shipment-date">Pending</span><span class="shipment-state">Undelivered</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="order-result">
        <strong class="result-incomplete">Incomplete</strong>
        <span><span class="qf-figure">1 / 2</span> items delivered</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="order-row">
      <strong class="order-id">A103</strong>
      <div class="shipments" role="group" aria-label="One item shipment">
        <span class="shipment on-time"><span class="shipment-date">Jan 31</span><span class="shipment-state">On time</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="order-result">
        <strong class="result-on-time">Complete on time</strong>
        <span><span class="qf-figure">1 / 1</span> item delivered</span>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="fulfillment-measures">
    <div class="measure shipment-measure">
      <strong class="measure-name">Delivered shipments on time</strong>
      <span class="measure-value qf-figure">83.3%</span>
      <div class="measure-bar shipment-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="late-segment"></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <span class="measure-formula"><span class="qf-figure">5</span> on time ÷ <span class="qf-figure">6</span> delivered</span>
      <p>This counts shipments and leaves the undelivered item out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure order-measure">
      <strong class="measure-name">Orders on time</strong>
      <span class="measure-value qf-figure">50%</span>
      <div class="measure-bar order-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span class="late-segment"></span><span class="pending-segment"></span><span></span></div>
      <span class="measure-formula"><span class="qf-figure">2</span> complete on time ÷ <span class="qf-figure">4</span> eligible</span>
      <p>Every eligible order counts, including the incomplete one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>An order counts as on time only when <strong>every item</strong> arrives by its original Jan <span class="qf-figure">31</span> promise. Each segment above represents one shipment or one order.</figcaption>
</figure>

